  "content": {
    "id": "p20-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "$x$ varies inversely with the cube of $y$. If $x=2$ when $y=3$, use a model to calculate $y$ when $x=16$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$y=\\dfrac32=1.5$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{k}{y^3}\\\\2&=\\frac{k}{3^3}\\\\k&=2\\times3^3\\\\k&=54\\end{align*}$$\nThe model is $x=\\dfrac{54}{y^3}$. When $x=16$:\n$$\\begin{align*}16&=\\frac{54}{y^3}\\\\y^3&=\\frac{54}{16}\\\\y^3&=\\frac{27}{8}\\\\y&=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{27}{8}}\\\\y&=\\frac32=1.5\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 47
  },
